{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about","id":430767,"title":"New to Forsaken 1.0 and totally new to 2.0; but what is 2.0 about?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-06T16:28:44-08:00","id":430767,"title":"New to Forsaken 1.0 and totally new to 2.0; but what is 2.0 about?","content":"I used to play Werewolf the Apocalypse back in the 90s with my buds I grew up with and have great memories doing so when home from college during summers and extended holiday seasons. Some of those memories lead me to feel like Werewolf : The Forsaken 1.0 was 'too evil' or we thought that the line had a too personal intent and horror which we didn't feel we wanted to have anything to do with... but now, in March 6th 2015 I am reading the PDF for Forsaken 1.0 and I can't believe I didn't give it a chance before now. I totally like it way better then the version back in the 90s and it's no less morally soul staining then any other RPG based on conflict with death as the usual main mechanic for ending the life of anything that gets in your way. <br /> <br /> So, I want to buy the print product of 1.0 Forsaken, but I just got wind that 2.0 came out as a PDF days ago as an 'advance product' and the FAQ says it's 4-6 six weeks for a vetting process before it comes out for Print-On-Demand... I am cool with the wait, but what does 2.0 have that would lure me away from 1.0 story and material. I just like everyone else, like shinny, novel things... but I sort of need to know without dumping $20 on another Forsaken PDF Product even if it is the newest one. <br /> <br /> <i><b>Can someone who has the 2.0 version give me a basic compare and contrast in a (of course limited and not comprehensive - unless of course you want to lay it all out) summary so I can judge to see if 1.0 is good enough to start with or whether 2.0 is going to be better </b></i>- it said it 're-imagined' the Tribes and such... how much is their a deviation, do you guys/gals like the change from 1.0 to 2.0 or what would you do in my shoes. <br /> <br /> I am not going to buy both at the start. I might buy 2.0 in a few months or a year later or so, or maybe I will only buy 2.0 as print and just keep my PDF of 1.0. I am a patient Aeternal <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and can wait on buying... especially since I its been 10 years out from when Forsaken was first released in 2005. What is remarkable is that the Forsaken released 2005 or so still speaks to me even though its definitely dated... that said, I kind of don't want to ruin that novel delight I got with it right now by grabbing 2.0 because 2.0 IS the newest shinny thing that this chattering monkey wants to bite - but since Forsaken 1.0 is only $25.99 Premium Color Print on Demand - it's a tough place to be.<br /> <br /> Thanks in Advance for any advice... insight into the different versions... and any other words that would help me.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b><sub>P.S - Where can one find some online games of Werewolf the Forsaken 1.0 or 2.0?</sub></b></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5256-aeternal","name":"Aeternal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T16:31:52-08:00","id":430787,"title":"","content":"If you like you can browse the Forsaken category of the blog where the developer, Stew Wilson, has been explaining the changes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/projects/werewolftheforsaken/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/projects/werewolftheforsaken/\" target=\"_blank\"> Werewolf: The Forsaken &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/projects/werewolftheforsaken/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/category/projects/werewolftheforsaken/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T17:38:36-08:00","id":430877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeternal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about#post430767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Can someone who has the 2.0 version give me a basic compare and contrast in a (of course limited and not comprehensive - unless of course you want to lay it all out) summary so I can judge to see if 1.0 is good enough to start with or whether 2.0 is going to be better </b></i>- it said it 're-imagined' the Tribes and such... how much is their a deviation, do you guys/gals like the change from 1.0 to 2.0 or what would you do in my shoes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't actually have the full PDF version of 2.0 quite yet, but I did write part of it, so maybe I can help. (Although, obviously, I may be a bit biased, so keep that in mind.)<br /> <br /> First, just a quick background so you know where I'm coming from. Like you, I played <b>Apocalypse</b> back in the day. It was what brought me into the WoD in the first place. You might say it was my first WoD love, so to speak. When <b>Forsaken</b> came around, I got excited all over again, due to the streamlining (five tribes instead of thirteen, for instance, and so on), the focus on the hunt, the change in tone, and the lack of metaplot. <br /> <br /> I ended up getting a copy of the First Edition core book at the Camarilla's Golden Ticket LARP '05 (holy shit that was a decade ago, I just realized). This was a month or two before it came out in general release, so I ate that thing right the hell up. I later served as a Forsaken Storyteller in some capacity at every single level of the club at the time (so, local/domain, regional, national, and global). Twice I held the regional and global positions simultaneously, which is just as exhausting as you'd think it is.<br /> <br /> I only say that so that when I say I love the hell out of this game, you know I mean it. Which brings us to Second Edition.<br /> <br /> <i>It is so much better.</i><br /> <br /> There is a much tighter focus on the Hunt in this edition. Our werewolves will find you. They will hunt you. And they will kill you. And they won't feel a single bit of doubt about it. Packs are terrifying - with an expansion that includes both wolf-blooded and human members of the extended pack, they could be anywhere, be anyone. <br /> <br /> Your tribe focuses you on a particular prey. Your Auspice dictates how you hunt that prey. A Rahu is certainly more straightforward than his Irraka packmate, but she'll just roll her eyes and hit the prey in its weak spot just when it isn't looking (or, more to the point, paying far more attention to the enraged wolf monster in front of it). Meanwhile, their Ithaeur has already bound spirits into her service to create a fetish to help kill or capture the prey, depending on the pack's goals.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the prey, they have more tools at their disposal. They won't go down without a fight. Happily, the Uratha have a new organization of Gifts and Facets that help alleviate the issues of the previous incarnation. Mechanically, the forms have more tools at their claws, in order to fulfill a variety of roles in the Hunt. <br /> <br /> The idigam themselves have also changed. They are the werewolves' &quot;out of context problem,&quot; and they have new rules and new abilities at their disposal. A collection of five sample idigam, complete with story hooks, backgrounds, stats, and more are in the book for your use if you like.<br /> <br /> As much as I loved the 1st Edition, I think 2nd Edition blows it out of the water. But that's just my opinion. I hope you check out the blog, and anything you can read up on it and make an informed decision for you and your group.<br /> <br /> But regardless of which edition you're playing, you're still playing <b>Forsaken</b>, so I think that's fantastic. Howl to the stars because you have prey to chase down!<br /> <br /> The Wolf Must Hunt.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T18:18:29-08:00","id":430956,"title":"","content":"I feel like it's worth clarifying that, unlike the different editions of oWoD, the 2nd edition books for the nWoD lines haven't thus far been that radically different from their previous editions in terms of the feel. Rather, each of the 2nd editions has refined the feel of the 1st edition, so there really isn't any reason to be wary of the 2nd edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T20:51:53-08:00","id":430968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=430956#post430956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like it's worth clarifying that, unlike the different editions of oWoD, the 2nd edition books for the nWoD lines haven't thus far been that radically different from their previous editions in terms of the feel. Rather, each of the 2nd editions has refined the feel of the 1st edition, so there really isn't any reason to be wary of the 2nd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage, it's more about highlighting what the game is about and cleaning up any of the oWoD flavoring that doesn't fit it.<br /> <br /> W:tF has always been about the Hunt but now that theme is more reflected via mechanics than the last one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T22:47:16-08:00","id":431074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=430877#post430877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I don't actually have the full PDF version of 2.0 quite yet, but I did write part of it, so maybe I can help. (Although, obviously, I may be a bit biased, so keep that in mind.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait.<br /> <br /> Stop.<br /> <br /> Rewind.<br /> <br /> How? Why? Whuh?(In regards to you not having a PDF of it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T23:20:25-08:00","id":431091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=431074#post431074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait.<br /> <br /> Stop.<br /> <br /> Rewind.<br /> <br /> How? Why? Whuh?(In regards to you not having a PDF of it)</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe writers that worked on it get a free copy, but they have not been sent out yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T23:22:15-08:00","id":431092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=431091#post431091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe writers that worked on it get a free copy, but they have not been sent out yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd figure the writers would be the first ones to get a copy, hence my confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T23:43:15-08:00","id":431122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=430956#post430956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like it's worth clarifying that, unlike the different editions of oWoD, the 2nd edition books for the nWoD lines haven't thus far been that radically different from their previous editions in terms of the feel. Rather, each of the 2nd editions has refined the feel of the 1st edition, so there really isn't any reason to be wary of the 2nd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is definitely more of a sense of honing in on what's thematically at the heart of each game, and cranking up the volume on THAT. For Werewolf that's &quot;the Hunt&quot;. For Mage it's &quot;Mystery&quot; and &quot;Hubris&quot;. For Vampire it's... well... the book was jokingly called &quot;SexMurder&quot; for a reason...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T00:39:16-08:00","id":431128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=431092#post431092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd figure the writers would be the first ones to get a copy, hence my confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sometimes takes a while for the comp copies to make their way through the arcane halls of OP distribution. Personally, I've sometimes had the pdf at the same time it went on sale, other times, it's taken a few days.<br /> <br /> We do have the 99% complete text for layout, but things can change between that and final product. Hence why we're a little cautious about saying exactly how things work, because some of us haven't yet seen what the final text is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T09:41:34-08:00","id":431282,"title":"","content":"Is there any plan to create an <b>Introductory Kit for Forsaken</b> (2nd ed.) like there was for <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/3370/Werewolf-the-Apocalypse--Free-Introductory-Kit\" target=\"_blank\">Apocalypse</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:25:18-08:00","id":431543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=431128#post431128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It sometimes takes a while for the comp copies to make their way through the arcane halls of OP distribution. Personally, I've sometimes had the pdf at the same time it went on sale, other times, it's taken a few days.<br /> <br /> We do have the 99% complete text for layout, but things can change between that and final product. Hence why we're a little cautious about saying exactly how things work, because some of us haven't yet seen what the final text is.</div> </div> </div> </div>This exactly. Which is why I've not really responded to much of anything of substance. (Well, that, or because Chris or Stew have already beaten me to it.) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T15:07:40-08:00","id":431818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=431282#post431282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any plan to create an <b>Introductory Kit for Forsaken</b> (2nd ed.) like there was for <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/3370/Werewolf-the-Apocalypse--Free-Introductory-Kit\" target=\"_blank\">Apocalypse</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at this time. I've batted around some ideas for an equivalent to <b>Reap the Whirlwind</b>, but we have no concrete plans at this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T18:55:19-07:00","id":433408,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the responses on my initial questions in the post and pointing me in directions that I can become more informed. Also, I must say, thanks for all the developer(s) and freelancers that helped write the book(s) over the years... especially those (thanks guys) that responded to this post. That is very well received by me. It surprised me and impressed me. I don't get 'surprised' very often anymore. Oh, one other question, one I asked but didn't get responded to yet: Is there a '<i><b>well known place</b></i>' for NewWoD (<i>online games - rpg</i>) <b>'looking for players</b>' and such? I know there is most likely ENWorld or a few other places that might have boards for it, but wanted to hear from the experienced and focused folks and fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5256-aeternal","name":"Aeternal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T19:24:56-07:00","id":433453,"title":"","content":"We've got boards here too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T19:36:45-07:00","id":433460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=430877#post430877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <i>It is so much better.</i><br /> <br /> There is a much tighter focus on the Hunt in this edition. Our werewolves will find you. They will hunt you. And they will kill you. And they won't feel a single bit of doubt about it. Packs are terrifying - with an expansion that includes both wolf-blooded and human members of the extended pack, they could be anywhere, be anyone.<br /> <br /> Your tribe focuses you on a particular prey. Your Auspice dictates how you hunt that prey. A Rahu is certainly more straightforward than his Irraka packmate, but she'll just roll her eyes and hit the prey in its weak spot just when it isn't looking (or, more to the point, paying far more attention to the enraged wolf monster in front of it). Meanwhile, their Ithaeur has already bound spirits into her service to create a fetish to help kill or capture the prey, depending on the pack's goals.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the prey, they have more tools at their disposal. They won't go down without a fight. Happily, the Uratha have a new organization of Gifts and Facets that help alleviate the issues of the previous incarnation. Mechanically, the forms have more tools at their claws, in order to fulfill a variety of roles in the Hunt.<br /> <br /> The idigam themselves have also changed. They are the werewolves' &quot;out of context problem,&quot; and they have new rules and new abilities at their disposal. A collection of five sample idigam, complete with story hooks, backgrounds, stats, and more are in the book for your use if you like.<br /> <br /> As much as I loved the 1st Edition, I think 2nd Edition blows it out of the water. But that's just my opinion. I hope you check out the blog, and anything you can read up on it and make an informed decision for you and your group.<br /> <br /> But regardless of which edition you're playing, you're still playing <b>Forsaken</b>, so I think that's fantastic. Howl to the stars because you have prey to chase down!<br /> <br /> The Wolf Must Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the write up about 2nd edition. So far, and it's a good read btw... I have been devouring 1st Edition as best I can being a PDF and I only have a PC - guess I am not part of the technocracy then since I am not reading this on an tablet... heh. So, from what others stated and what you wrote I get the impression that 2nd Edition emphasizes more of the 'feel and emotion' of 1st Edition and also '<b>streamlines the play</b>' for more of what maybe you guys polled and used accurate anecdotal research over 10 years of feedback and play?<br /> <br /> What do you all mean when you say '<b>the feeling</b>' and me adding an assumed '<b>emotion</b>' with it? How much more clear can you make it that this is a game about horror as a metaTheme? The gamemaster's section has a LOT of info and it is clear that it's about the horror - it is so very well done. The OLD WoD Werewolf 2nd Edition version was also about cosmic-horror and that metaPlot and metaTheme worked for us at the time, unfortunately, my old group is too nostalgic for the OWoD and no interest in the new line. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Part of that has to do with the fact that my group at the time had more interest in defending the world and less about personal explorations into what horror was and is... even though it saturated the product - it was a given but could be secondary and at least for me it was.<br /> <br /> Well... I am new to the NewWoD, hell it's only been ten years before I got curious enough to check it out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So thanks thus far for all the help people have given me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5256-aeternal","name":"Aeternal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T23:50:00-07:00","id":435385,"title":"","content":"Well that was nice... I had a long response here but then it crashed... So here is a shorter version.<br /> <br /> I am an cWoD veteran who never really liked the nWoD as it came out, with the exception of CtL which I played with cWoD rules, as I disliked the rules and to me they felt way too similar to the cWoD versions, with the exception of Lost which is why I liked it despite being a huge fan of Dreaming as well. Now with the second editions, or rather the GMC God-Machine Chronicle, update on the rules system it has finally become something interesting and something I can work with, I love it's beat and conditions system which is very similar to Fate if your familiar with that system, another reason why the 2nd editions have managed to win me over is the purging of cWoD elements from them, well at least as much of them as they have been able to get away with we still have the Ventrue and the Gangrel in nWoD and similar Disciplines though they have taken a welcome twist away from their predecessors and similarly we still have the spirit world in Forsaken ( I would have felt it better to not have it in the new game about werewolves as it was so central to Apocalypse but that boat sailed 10 years ago) but otherwise it seeks to widen the gap between it and Apocalypse coming into it's own more clearly.<br /> <br /> So to summarise A n cWoD player, ST and a fan I heartily recommend going with the 2nd editions over the first.<br /> <br /> Gotta admit I am still reading through the WtF 2nd but so far I have liked it and the fact that they downplay the spirit cop side a bit and emphasize the need to hunt more though I still have a few issues with it like why would anyone join in these tribes and responsibilities instead of just going basically Ghost Wolf, but perhaps it is clarified as I read further, and I did notice that there are mechanical advantages in belonging to a tribe but I am talking from an IC point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T00:01:04-07:00","id":435397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=435385#post435385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still have a few issues with it like why would anyone join in these tribes and responsibilities instead of just going basically Ghost Wolf, but perhaps it is clarified as I read further, and I did notice that there are mechanical advantages in belonging to a tribe but I am talking from an IC point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you join forums on the internet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T00:50:04-07:00","id":435440,"title":"","content":"It's also worth considering, especially for the IC perspective, that most Uratha are taught by other Uratha or Wolf-blooded about what they are. And they're going to teach them that joining a Tribe the best thing to do. There's going to be plenty of social pressure to join a Tribe rather than going Ghost Wolf. Tribes are about giving your hunt purpose (or at a minimum are going to be sold that way IC) and going Ghost Wolf means you're choosing to hunt without a purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T09:27:02-07:00","id":435825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=435385#post435385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta admit I am still reading through the WtF 2nd but so far I have liked it and the fact that they downplay the spirit cop side a bit and emphasize the need to hunt more though I still have a few issues with it like why would anyone join in these tribes and responsibilities instead of just going basically Ghost Wolf, but perhaps it is clarified as I read further, and I did notice that there are mechanical advantages in belonging to a tribe but I am talking from an IC point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>You just discovered you turn into a giant furry rage monster and can see things nobody else can see (that want to hurt you). Most people are gonna be keen to join a group who knows what they are going through and can teach them how to deal with it. Folks going it alone are going to be relatively rare and often because of circumstance (nobody comes forward to help).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T10:03:49-07:00","id":435864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=435385#post435385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that was nice... I had a long response here but then it crashed... So here is a shorter version.<br /> <br /> I am an cWoD veteran who never really liked the nWoD as it came out, with the exception of CtL which I played with cWoD rules, as I disliked the rules and to me they felt way too similar to the cWoD versions, with the exception of Lost which is why I liked it despite being a huge fan of Dreaming as well. Now with the second editions, or rather the GMC God-Machine Chronicle, update on the rules system it has finally become something interesting and something I can work with, I love it's beat and conditions system which is very similar to Fate if your familiar with that system, another reason why the 2nd editions have managed to win me over is the purging of cWoD elements from them, well at least as much of them as they have been able to get away with we still have the Ventrue and the Gangrel in nWoD and similar Disciplines though they have taken a welcome twist away from their predecessors and similarly we still have the spirit world in Forsaken ( I would have felt it better to not have it in the new game about werewolves as it was so central to Apocalypse but that boat sailed 10 years ago) but otherwise it seeks to widen the gap between it and Apocalypse coming into it's own more clearly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The new Editions, while having awesome fluff, have mechanics that (in my opinion) far inferior to the Fate Mechanics, though. While similar, they fill a slightly different niche. And Fate does it better in my opinion. That said, you cannot beat the Fluff that Onyx Path is producing, anywhere... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T03:09:30-07:00","id":438226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why do you join forums on the internet? </div> </div> </div>To talk about things with like minded people generally. Not to plot about killing people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also worth considering, especially for the IC perspective, that most Uratha are taught by other Uratha or Wolf-blooded about what they are. And they're going to teach them that joining a Tribe the best thing to do. There's going to be plenty of social pressure to join a Tribe rather than going Ghost Wolf. Tribes are about giving your hunt purpose (or at a minimum are going to be sold that way IC) and going Ghost Wolf means you're choosing to hunt without a purpose. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You just discovered you turn into a giant furry rage monster and can see things nobody else can see (that want to hurt you). Most people are gonna be keen to join a group who knows what they are going through and can teach them how to deal with it. Folks going it alone are going to be relatively rare and often because of circumstance (nobody comes forward to help). </div> </div> </div>Well if you look at the Tribes, and the Oath of the Moon only makes matters worse but more on that later, from a perspective of normal human being they start to look like a bunch of complete psychos. Let's say you just recovered from your first change and have some blood on your hands and your feelings conflicted as some part of you, some animalistic instinct, growls in satisfaction while your human side, you know the one you have had all your life, if likely horrified and feeling immense amounts of guilt. Then this guy comes along to you and tells you that your a werewolf and so is he, he also says it's ok to kill someone because you know the Wolf Must Hunt. Then he tells you about the Tribes which include these guys who kill our own People, yes they dedicate their lives to killing other Werewolves, these guys who go around killing spirits and these others who generally act like leatherface and go after these rat/spider spirit things, then there's the Tribe dedicated to murdering humans, yes your fellow humans with whom you have been raised their nice hunting you know so don't worry about the fellow you just mauled, and then there are these guys who hunt those human possessed by spirits or those about to be possessed. Then he goes on telling you about the laws of your kind which are pretty simple there is only one commandment agaisnt killing and thats that you shouldn't kill other Werewolves, but wait didn't you just tell me there was a whole Tribe dedicated to just that, nor should you eat humans cause you know cannibalism is bad, what the hell by calling it cannibalism you also say humans are our people as well and we still hunt them wasn't that first law against people hunting people again. After listening to a clearly mad person telling you all this would you really want to join that club? Add to this if he starts ranting about history and how your people committed patricide and now you'll have to take up the responsibilities of that dead spirit wolf and that's why you should hunt and kill those your Tribe does, because they take orders apparently from some ancient patricidal spirits.<br /> <br /> I really, really, do not see why someone would join a Tribe without at the least trying it out on his own. And for many that could even in a way, though they would not have a normal life by any means, be a successful way to live.<br /> <br /> I can always suspend my disbelief of course and create a character that belongs to one of the Tribes, and would happily do so in most cases, but should an ST ever start a story where we begin as humans I really can't see myself realistically joining up in that mad house unless I was already playing a slightly psychotic or sociopathic fellow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T05:30:30-07:00","id":438294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=438226#post438226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &lt;<i>snip</i>&gt;<br /> <br /> I really, really, do not see why someone would join a Tribe without at the least trying it out on his own. And for many that could even in a way, though they would not have a normal life by any means, be a successful way to live.<br /> <br /> I can always suspend my disbelief of course and create a character that belongs to one of the Tribes, and would happily do so in most cases, but should an ST ever start a story where we begin as humans I really can't see myself realistically joining up in that mad house unless I was already playing a slightly psychotic or sociopathic fellow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tribes provide a context and support network for dealing with how your life has been turned upside-down, while also giving you a group of acceptable targets for your new urges to hunt. And they're intense urges, too: At Primal Urge 1, you have to hunt something at least once every 3 months or possibly gain Harmony. This in turn means you may start raging more often as your character tries <i>so hard</i> to deny their spirit self.<br /> <br /> Also, they don't tell you &quot;It's okay to kill someone.&quot; Not all Hunts have to end with a killing. A good example might be starting a grassroots movement to get a corrupt politician kicked out of office by electing a new one. Maybe you want a Spirit to teach you a new Gift: declare a hunt on it, no reason to offend the Shadow Courts by slaying it. Your idiot nephew went and joined a Fire-Touched Pack that your protectorate has a cease-fire deal with and attacking them directly might start a bloody and costly war: Declare a hunt on him so you can drag his ass back home and learn him some sense, dagummit!<br /> <br /> I'm sure plenty of tribal members behave in sociopathic ways, and tribes may paint each other in wide, stereotypical strokes, but at the end of the day Tribes are a combination of support group and brotherhood, and that's a very enticing prospect for a freshly Changed Uratha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T05:45:10-07:00","id":438299,"title":"","content":"I think that's a great example of how you don't pitch tribal membership. A lot of Ghost Wolves probably come from botched initiations where the Werewolf doing the greeting and instruction didn't ease a first changer into the life well enough. Its also possible that with the psychological changes that take place during the period leading up to the first change, most new Werewolves are already mentally and emotionally ready to listen to the first person who can offer some meaning to all of this without looking too closely at the fine print. In other words the urge may be overwhelming to be part of a greater identity now that the ways a person identified themselves in the human race don't have quite the same urgency. Something has to go in the space left by politics, religion etc so in time as a new Werewolf adjusts, that would be tribes and lodges. I doubt most successful recruitments involve being up front with the full ramifications of what Werewolf society is like while someone is still washing the blood out of their mouth. Unless of course something changes within a person during the first change to make them more inclined to think its reasonable. I'm betting this is one of those areas where players choose whether becoming a Werewolf programs a person to want to join a Tribe or if its more like joining a cult: once you've been entrusted with the sacred knowledge that god wants you to kill humans, you're already a true believer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T06:45:45-07:00","id":438331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=438226#post438226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Add to this if he starts ranting about history and how your people committed patricide and now you'll have to take up the responsibilities of that dead spirit wolf and that's why you should hunt and kill those your Tribe does, because they take orders apparently from some ancient patricidal spirits.<br /> <br /> I really, really, do not see why someone would join a Tribe without at the least trying it out on his own. And for many that could even in a way, though they would not have a normal life by any means, be a successful way to live.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to have an overall negative view of the tribes, which probably isn't helping.<br /> <br /> You don't take up responsibilities just because of patricide killed eons ago. You take it up because you're part spirit of the hunt, and if you don't feed that part of yourself you're going to go mad. Just like we in the real world desire companionship and other needs, the wolf must hunt. And you don't have to hunt just what your tribe hunts, you and your pack decide what to hunt depending on what's causing trouble for them, and what they think needs to be done. If they think they're do-gooders, they might focus on killing things they think are bad, drug dealers, 'evil' spirits and so forth. If they're more ambitious they might just hunt powerful foes. If they refuse to kill people, they could focus on the most monstrous of creatures, the claimed and hosts and hive-claimed. Your tribe only determines what you're trained to hunt, it doesn't force you to hunt that kind of thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T09:06:09-07:00","id":438505,"title":"","content":"@Possessed:<br /> <br /> Somebody doesn't seems to be emotionally mature enough to understand the nuances of what constitutes hunting in Forsaken. <b>Protip:</b> It's not the same as murder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T09:17:03-07:00","id":438514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=438505#post438505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's not the same as murder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. the 3 dot Gibbous Moon gift seems especially useful for a pack who merely wish to scare the living shit out of their target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-12-2015, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T09:18:47-07:00","id":438517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=438505#post438505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Possessed:<br /> <br /> Somebody doesn't seems to be emotionally mature enough to understand the nuances of what constitutes hunting in Forsaken. <b>Protip:</b> It's not the same as murder.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Personal attacks are against the forum rules. Feel free to express you opinions, but please do so without calling other users emotionally immature.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T00:33:03-07:00","id":439554,"title":"","content":"Well I have a thicker skin than that Charlaquin but I do appreciate the shining armour, looks good on you.<br /> <br /> Anyway I'll take up these notions individually and comment each in turn. Though first of all, since to me the attitude seems rather defensive around here as if I were bashing the game and it's world (which I assure you I am not, so far I'm rather liking the book), I would like to note that these are issues which might not be issues to you who have played the game for several years and how they are represented here now may not be how you were presented with them originally. I am seeing all of this with fresh eyes and my reaction come not from already knowing the tribes inside and out, and thus able to fill in the possible blanks left by the actual book some of that may even come unconsciously, but from a perspective of someone new to the line. As a side note such accusations of immaturity while a non-issue for me personally, you really would need to try harder to offend me, is something that a new player, especially one new to the hobby, might not take so well and such behaviour gives a bad impression of the community. But such hubris as shown here is really familiar to me as well, when commenting on lines I know well as with cWoD, though I try my best to steer away from attacking the person and rather correcting them in the matter, sometimes sternly sometimes not depending upon my own mood and hurry usually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that's a great example of how you don't pitch tribal membership. A lot of Ghost Wolves probably come from botched initiations where the Werewolf doing the greeting and instruction didn't ease a first changer into the life well enough. Its also possible that with the psychological changes that take place during the period leading up to the first change, most new Werewolves are already mentally and emotionally ready to listen to the first person who can offer some meaning to all of this without looking too closely at the fine print. </div> </div> </div>I agree, my example was rather simplifying to illustrate my point as clearly as possible, in that many Ghost Wolves like are that because their indoctrinator might be an Uratha who already is so comfortable with his role or just isn't the best manipulator around in which case the young wolf might not quite like what he hears. As I take it that the moments after the First Change, and perhaps even few first weeks after it, are a confusing time at best when the Urdur is still struggling with his human rationality and upbringing versus the newly found wolf instincts. During this conflict it probably doesn't require that much, perhaps a single mistakenly put word or two, to drive the young one away.<br /> Also after the change, especially a violent one, it is a bit hard I'd imagine to come up to the newly changed Urdur and start going more deeply into the meaning of the word Hunt for most people hunting means going after something and killing it either for food, protection of self and community or for other goods gained from the carcass when standing there your hands dripping fresh blood, figuratively the act is easily (even though their psychological makeup is also going through a change of it's own) traumatizing enough that it feels fresh for a long time, it is kinda hard to think that hunting could also mean catch and release type of action. Like said I am looking at this not from a point of view of an experienced Uratha nor of an expert of their lore but from the IC point of view of the poor bastard who really has a hard time getting what he is going thru and is likely horrified at the prospect. True some might be of such nature that they cling to the first person to approach them and are ready to sign anything without looking at the fine print, if they look at the contract at all, but some, many I would hope for the sake of mankind, are able to hold themselves together enough to think about this rationally and quite frankly the Tribe descriptions do not give a good picture of them, from a human point of view.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You seem to have an overall negative view of the tribes, which probably isn't helping. </div> </div> </div>Probably true but my view of them is colored only by how they are described in the book in their own splat pages. While I get the description if I go into the predator thought mode they seem rather horrid bunch one and all if looking at it through purely human eyes. Don't know if you have a different view of them through other books or because you have become used to them as institutions, and since you have for a long time been looking it all through experienced Urathas eyes. And it doesn't help that the Oath of the Moon includes a prohibition of people killing people but then there is a Tribe that does just that, and yes hunting may not mean killing all the time but be honest with me now in this case it often does doesn't it? Blood Talons are at the least written in a way that such is the first impression one get's from them, while they may not hunt and kill the Forsaken they do so for the Pure, or that is the understanding I got from their Tribe splat. Also it doesn't help that it is very much emphasized there how the other Tribes are somewhat distrustful of them because they think them as killers of other Uratha.<br /> <br /> I get that the tribes start to sound a lot more enticing after you have been changed for a while and have become familiar with your instincts, and even possibly come to face the negative consequences of trying to fight the urges and so on, but I would think that would be after several months, at the least, or most likely years of trying to find your own way, and not necessarily even then if you have managed to find your own way of handling things. But at some point after months/years of experience as an Uratha you might start to be ready to join one of them for the company, or gather up other Ghost Wolves for company, but I am talking of freshly changed Urdur in my original post.<br /> <br /> And like said I am more than able to suspend my disbelief at the first moments, or just create enough of a bastard characters that accepting these things is easy, of my characters Change and indoctrination to create a Tribe member. And I am fond of Iron Masters for example, despite or because they hunt humans I am not sure.<br /> <br /> Also as a final note I ma not some treehugging friendly type who is horrified by the actions of the Uratha if you have read my post on the cWoD side you would know that I am one of those who like to play Nephandi, Baali or other beings who might flay you in the name of greater good, that is their for their own good, and still make an interesting character about it but like I would have a hard time believing any of them able to recruit majority of random group of people into agreeing with them I also have a hard time believing that the wast majority of those going through the first change are ready to join Tribes instead of going at it alone and/or with their normal support group.<br /> <br /> I like the game and the fluff, apart from my own desire to not have these Werewolves as well tied to the spirit world, and have enjoyed what I have read thus far but these are a brutal People and the book does an excellent job at portraying that so good in fact that it does make one think who in their right mind, or even in a wrong one, would voluntarily join up with these folks unless they have already at the least tried to work on it alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm betting this is one of those areas where players choose whether becoming a Werewolf programs a person to want to join a Tribe or if its more like joining a cult: once you've been entrusted with the sacred knowledge that god wants you to kill humans, you're already a true believer. </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly so. The book doesn't -at least clearly- say, that they would immediately gain a such a need to join with something that they would be willing to go with the first person who comes along and I would think such an artificial component to the forming of Tribes would be both unnecessary and inelegant solution. So that leaves us with the Cult type introdiction which comes with it's own troubles, including that Cults tend to usually be successful in indoctrinating a certain type of people, and while the Urdur is definitely confused and looking for answers I would think most would still have enough of an identity and will of their own to not eat it all up with the hook, line and sinker. Though this approach would likely be the best one I still find it statistically odd that they would manage to get the majority of the newly changed into the fold right a way.<br /> <br /> As a side note I have similar thoughts of WtA's Tribes and Garou but there you are often, unless your a lost cub, indoctrinated by one or both of your own parents and you may even have been raised to be ready for this possibility. But now in WtF there is this whole &quot;Tribe&quot; of wolves, this implies that they too are quite numerous, who reject the normal Tribes and go on it alone and that makes it overall even harder to see a reason for giving up on everything in your old life to join up with a bunch of strangers who have certain sociopathic tendencies.<br /> <br /> And like said Oath of the Moon doesn't really help the matter either as there is no law in it against killing, except other Werewolves which creates it's own problems when the Blood Talons are a thing, only against eating humans/wolves. That in itself implies, it pretty much downright says, that this is a society where killing is acceptable. And not only that but htey draw the line on eating your victim. Up to and until that point everything is just fine and dandy according to their laws. Now try to take all that in through fresh eyes from a perspective of someone who feels the conflicted emotions of guilt mixed with a feeling of exhilarating freedom and who doesn't know about the bad sides of resisting these urges yet and you should start to see how odd it should feel from an IC perspective. It should feel like your going insane gaining some sick enjoyment from hunting and killing others, colored by the feelings of guilt from your human upbringing, and that these People offering to help have fallen of that wagon a long time ago into accepting their insanity and just letting go. The human reaction is to reach for something familiar and to resist that fall into those feelings that you think as insane. Joining a Tribe seems like an act of letting go and reaching for the unknown which is pretty rare way to go about things.<br /> <br /> I have no difficulties in seeing how nuanced hunting is for the Forsaken, or all the meanings they might put behind the word but then again I have read a manual about them and their kind while the poor recruit has not and he is likely not in a calm enough mood to reflect on all the possible meanings of the word hunt. I am not looking at this from the perspective of a player but of a poor unfortunate character put into that situation.<br /> <br /> But enough of my ramblings I do think I have made my point clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T01:51:45-07:00","id":439620,"title":"","content":"<b>Possessed</b>,<br /> <br /> If I am to understand this correctly then there wouldn't be any reason why this character idea of your's wouldn't become a Ghost Wolf than joining the other Tribes. In the write up for the Ghost Wolves themselves they do a really good job of conveying that a majority of the Tribeless are just poor souls who are trying to hold on to the person they were while coping with the Primal Urge that now burn within their souls telling them to <i>hunt, hunt, HUNT,</i> until the Death Rage overcomes them and the Wolf prowls once more. My favorite part in the Ghost Wolf write up is where the narrator is talking about a serial killer in the paper and how he's certain he could track them down and bring them to justice, especially how good it would feel to end such a monster when they could easily do so now. <br /> <br /> This kind of internal struggle has never been such a viable charcter option than it is now in 2E and this is why the Ghost Wolves are so cool. Especially when you get to Ghost Wolf Lodges and how vastly different they are from the more formal Tribe Lodges.<br /> <br /> Then again, I am a Tribe person myself. There are 101 different things in the World of Darkness that either want to kill or eat your character (Not necessarily in that order) and when surrounded by monsters that voice inside urging you on becomes ever more so difficult to ignore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T02:09:39-07:00","id":439633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I am to understand this correctly then there wouldn't be any reason why this character idea of your's wouldn't become a Ghost Wolf than joining the other Tribes. </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is my point except that I do think that majority of newly Changed would rather go Ghost Wolf than join another Tribe as they sound pretty disturbing from an IC point of view mostly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This kind of internal struggle has never been such a viable charcter option than it is now in 2E and this is why the Ghost Wolves are so cool. Especially when you get to Ghost Wolf Lodges and how vastly different they are from the more formal Tribe Lodges. </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then again, I am a Tribe person myself. There are 101 different things in the World of Darkness that either want to kill or eat your character (Not necessarily in that order) and when surrounded by monsters that voice inside urging you on becomes ever more so difficult to ignore. </div> </div> </div>Also agreed. My point is that Ghost Wolf, to me at least, sounds the most logical way for <i><b>most</b></i> Urdur to choose for their few first years at the least and start thinking of the other Tribes as possibilities only after they have gone through that transition period where they come to terms with themselves and who they are.<br /> <br /> For example the one spoken of in the Ghost Wolf splat who looks at that serial killer he might hunt him down as a special case and then try to go on with his life, or he might end up eating the poor bugger which would lead to it's own problems or he would find a purpose there and either remain at that path as a Ghost Wolf or slowly flow towards joining the Iron Masters. The things is that he probably wouldn't have chosen that path right after the change it takes time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T02:15:40-07:00","id":439638,"title":"","content":"You do get to decide a couple of breaking points yourself. If you want to play a character who is against killing humans, you can totally do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T02:22:52-07:00","id":439641,"title":"","content":"Ah I'm starting to see what you're saying.<br /> <br /> In that regards I believe a majority of the newly First Changed end up in the Tribs of the Moon or the Pure mostly for two reasons.<br /> <br /> 1. They are found by someone who belongs to one of those Tribes already and are quickly indoctronated to their cause, and let's be realistic in that this wouldn't be that hard a sell too. No matter how pure of heart the individual is half of who they are now is totally into what all of the Tribes are selling (that's just the tragic nature of their dualistic spirit.)<br /> <br /> 2. Resources. Pure and simple. Just like the Covenants and Orders in the other game lines the Tribes of the Moon and Pure are way more organized and unified than the individual Ghost Wolves and their scattered Lodges. A single Pack of Storm Lords can bring more resources to bear against their enemies than the most wealthy of Ghost Wolves simply due to the fact that they have a far richer history and network of allies to draw from than the lone wolves of the World of Darkness. (Important to note though that this doesn't make the small Pack of Storm Lords more powerful than this expert Ghost Wolf, just that the hunt of the Tribless will be much more perilous. And according to custom make the Storm Lords respect that Ghost Wolf that much more for it's dedication and fortitude.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T03:03:00-07:00","id":439672,"title":"","content":"Two things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=438226#post438226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Add to this if he starts ranting about history and how your people committed patricide and now you'll have to take up the responsibilities of that dead spirit wolf and that's why you should hunt and kill those your Tribe does, because they take orders apparently from some ancient patricidal spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Firstborn, according to legend, did not commit patricide. The First Pack did. Werewolves, not spirits. This is a common confusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can always suspend my disbelief of course and create a character that belongs to one of the Tribes, and would happily do so in most cases, but should an ST ever start a story where we begin as humans I really can't see myself realistically joining up in that mad house unless I was already playing a slightly psychotic or sociopathic fellow. </div> </div> </div>From a human perspective, sure, werewolves probably do look at least slightly (if not very) psychotic. I mean, they have to hunt every so often, they can be (but aren't necessarily) xenophobic, they have basically zero issue with killing for the most part...so yeah. But then, werewolves aren't human. They no longer necessarily adhere to human mores. What's psychotic for a human is perfectly valid and acceptable behavior for a werewolf. That's why they're monsters.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T04:59:23-07:00","id":439773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=439672#post439672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Firstborn, according to legend, did not commit patricide. The First Pack did. Werewolves, not spirits. This is a common confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>But now in 2ed theyn did, page 64:<br /> &quot;Only a killing blow would do, and so the Uratha \u2014 and five<br /> of the greatest wolf spirits \u2014 went for Urfarah\u2019s throat.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T08:39:28-07:00","id":439963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=439633#post439633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that Ghost Wolf, to me at least, sounds the most logical way for <i><b>most</b></i> Urdur to choose for their few first years at the least and start thinking of the other Tribes as possibilities only after they have gone through that transition period where they come to terms with themselves and who they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see a few problems with this.<br /> <br /> First off, &quot;logical&quot; seems a bit misplaced. What makes the most logical sense from an external perspective isn't the same as what makes the most logical sense form an internal perspective. &quot;I'll take a few years to find myself,&quot; does not seem like a logical thought for a freshly changed werewolf to have. They just turned into a monster that can, at any moment, flip out and kill everyone around them. The immediacy of their situation doesn't really logically lead to taking a lot of time to figure things out for themselves; unless they are actual sociopaths that don't care that come to terms with themselves in their own time will probably mean the deaths of dozens of people.<br /> <br /> Second, it seems to assume that the First Change is both more abrupt and less complete than the book presents. The book doesn't portray this as, &quot;one day you were normal, then bam one night you change into a werewolf with a completely human mind, now go from there.&quot; The book describes there being considerable psychological lead up to it, as well as significant psychological changes that go along with the First Change. After the First Change a new werewolf sees the world through the eyes of a werewolf, not a human. Their base biological urges change and their psychology with it. The urge to be with other people that understand what you are, and what you're going through, is going to be incredibly strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T08:51:37-07:00","id":439975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=439554#post439554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I have a thicker skin than that Charlaquin but I do appreciate the shining armour, looks good on you.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>My god! Its almost like Moderators are supposed to enforce the established rules of the community!<br /> Take a week off. </b></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T09:00:27-07:00","id":439988,"title":"","content":"The way I like to present it is that most newly first changed werewolves don't immediately join a Tribe. The books do say that the Uratha and the Pure keep tabs on wolf blooded who may be on the verge of their first change and approach them right away, but for reasons similar to yours, I don't imagine that would generally be well-received. In my games, the tribes are well aware of that, and tend to leave the new werewolf alone for a few weeks, to give them time to process what's happened and start getting used to their new predatory urges. Obviously, they monitor the pup closely during this time, so they can intervene if they get themselves into trouble, or if the other side tries to get to them first. During this period, the new werewolf is likely a murder suspect, which is sure to add a lot of stress, and potential death rage triggers. Their whole life is falling apart around them, they're seeing spirits that constantly harras them, and all the while they have a near irresistible urge to hunt and to kill. THAT's when the tribes' representatives come to them, and offer purpose, clarity, and a way to realize those predatory urges <i>without</i> hurting people they care about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T13:17:25-07:00","id":440393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=439554#post439554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I have a thicker skin than that Charlaquin but I do appreciate the shining armour, looks good on you.<br /> <br /> Anyway I'll take up these notions individually and comment each in turn. Though first of all, since to me the attitude seems rather defensive around here as if I were bashing the game and it's world (which I assure you I am not, so far I'm rather liking the book), I would like to note that these are issues which might not be issues to you who have played the game for several years and how they are represented here now may not be how you were presented with them originally. I am seeing all of this with fresh eyes and my reaction come not from already knowing the tribes inside and out, and thus able to fill in the possible blanks left by the actual book some of that may even come unconsciously, but from a perspective of someone new to the line. As a side note such accusations of immaturity while a non-issue for me personally, you really would need to try harder to offend me, is something that a new player, especially one new to the hobby, might not take so well and such behaviour gives a bad impression of the community. But such hubris as shown here is really familiar to me as well, when commenting on lines I know well as with cWoD, though I try my best to steer away from attacking the person and rather correcting them in the matter, sometimes sternly sometimes not depending upon my own mood and hurry usually.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't know saying someone seemed to be immature in outlook or demeanor was a personal attack. Better add that to the ToS, guys. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=439554#post439554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, my example was rather simplifying to illustrate my point as clearly as possible, in that many Ghost Wolves like are that because their indoctrinator might be an Uratha who already is so comfortable with his role or just isn't the best manipulator around in which case the young wolf might not quite like what he hears. As I take it that the moments after the First Change, and perhaps even few first weeks after it, are a confusing time at best when the Urdur is still struggling with his human rationality and upbringing versus the newly found wolf instincts. During this conflict it probably doesn't require that much, perhaps a single mistakenly put word or two, to drive the young one away.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, your example was more like a dramatic failure in a persuasion attempt. It wasn't a simplification, it was downright satirical. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=439554#post439554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also after the change, especially a violent one, it is a bit hard I'd imagine to come up to the newly changed Urdur and start going more deeply into the meaning of the word Hunt for most people hunting means going after something and killing it either for food, protection of self and community or for other goods gained from the carcass when standing there your hands dripping fresh blood, figuratively the act is easily (even though their psychological makeup is also going through a change of it's own) traumatizing enough that it feels fresh for a long time, it is kinda hard to think that hunting could also mean catch and release type of action. Like said I am looking at this not from a point of view of an experienced Uratha nor of an expert of their lore but from the IC point of view of the poor bastard who really has a hard time getting what he is going thru and is likely horrified at the prospect. True some might be of such nature that they cling to the first person to approach them and are ready to sign anything without looking at the fine print, if they look at the contract at all, but some, many I would hope for the sake of mankind, are able to hold themselves together enough to think about this rationally and quite frankly the Tribe descriptions do not give a good picture of them, from a human point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>This assumes that you First Changed say, in your childhood home and slaughtered your family, for example. What if your victim(s) where Claimed, Hosts, Spirits or another Werewolf? Have a Blood Talon tell an Iron Master he should kill off a whole squad of SWAT to deal with that issue, as if that wouldn't escalate things on a domestic terrorist man-hunt for you and/or your pack. The Iron Master would blow the Talon off. You don't hunt humanity like you do a gazelle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=439554#post439554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably true but my view of them is colored only by how they are described in the book in their own splat pages. While I get the description if I go into the predator thought mode they seem rather horrid bunch one and all if looking at it through purely human eyes. Don't know if you have a different view of them through other books or because you have become used to them as institutions, and since you have for a long time been looking it all through experienced Urathas eyes. And it doesn't help that the Oath of the Moon includes a prohibition of people killing people but then there is a Tribe that does just that, and yes hunting may not mean killing all the time but be honest with me now in this case it often does doesn't it? Blood Talons are at the least written in a way that such is the first impression one get's from them, while they may not hunt and kill the Forsaken they do so for the Pure, or that is the understanding I got from their Tribe splat. Also it doesn't help that it is very much emphasized there how the other Tribes are somewhat distrustful of them because they think them as killers of other Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Murder. The prohibition is to Murder. Killing is fine. <b>Murder</b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> is the killing of another person without </span></span></span><i><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justification_(jurisprudence)\" target=\"_blank\">justification</a></i><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> or valid </span></span><i><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Excuse_(legal)\" target=\"_blank\">excuse</a></i>. Blood Talons are all about enforcing the Oath. This misunderstanding is why you cannot grasp the issue.<br /> <br /> If you're say, Shaolin and the notion of killing a cockroach bothers you because it might be someone's next life...<br /> <br /> Soldiers aren't murderers, they have a duty which invariably involves killing, and their job isn't a valid excuse to prosecute them, for instance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=439554#post439554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that the tribes start to sound a lot more enticing after you have been changed for a while and have become familiar with your instincts, and even possibly come to face the negative consequences of trying to fight the urges and so on, but I would think that would be after several months, at the least, or most likely years of trying to find your own way, and not necessarily even then if you have managed to find your own way of handling things. But at some point after months/years of experience as an Uratha you might start to be ready to join one of them for the company, or gather up other Ghost Wolves for company, but I am talking of freshly changed Urdur in my original post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno man. Tribes start to sound fucking amazing the second I learn there's a whole tribe out there who hunts down those fucking spiders that ate my sister's brains. Or the fucking spirits that wore my dad like a sock puppet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=439554#post439554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And like said I am more than able to suspend my disbelief at the first moments, or just create enough of a bastard characters that accepting these things is easy, of my characters Change and indoctrination to create a Tribe member. And I am fond of Iron Masters for example, despite or because they hunt humans I am not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you are thinking way too literally. Humans gather in institutions and groups. Iron Masters learned all the tricks in the book to herd those like we do with cattle. There's a reason Uratha call them Herd. There's also the point that Herd animals, when terrified, stampede.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=439554#post439554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also as a final note I ma not some treehugging friendly type who is horrified by the actions of the Uratha if you have read my post on the cWoD side you would know that I am one of those who like to play Nephandi, Baali or other beings who might flay you in the name of greater good, that is their for their own good, and still make an interesting character about it <b>but like I would have a hard time believing any of them able to recruit majority of random group of people into agreeing with them I also have a hard time believing that the vast majority of those going through the first change are ready to join Tribes instead of going at it alone and/or with their normal support group.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>And you would be correct. Your mistake lies in believing that fresh Nuzusul jump into tribes the following day of their first change. Nevermind their state of mind, they aren't nowhere near prepared to what a rite of initiation would entail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=439554#post439554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The book doesn't -at least clearly- say, that they would immediately gain a such a need to join with something that they would be willing to go with the first person who comes along and I would think such an artificial component to the forming of Tribes would be both unnecessary and inelegant solution.</b> So that leaves us with the Cult type introdiction which comes with it's own troubles, including that Cults tend to usually be successful in indoctrinating a certain type of people, and while the Urdur is definitely confused and looking for answers I would think most would still have enough of an identity and will of their own to not eat it all up with the hook, line and sinker. Though this approach would likely be the best one I still find it statistically odd that they would manage to get the majority of the newly changed into the fold right a way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is in your own imagination. Literally, the last thing I would have a character with the slightless semblance of social acuity or empathy would be to start blabbing about how fucking amazing is to pledge your spirit-stuff to the wolf-deity that would end the world in some myths to someone who just butchered his or her significant other two hours ago, and doesn't even remembers but that can smell him/her in his bloodied limbs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=439554#post439554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side note I have similar thoughts of WtA's Tribes and Garou but there you are often, unless your a lost cub, indoctrinated by one or both of your own parents and you may even have been raised to be ready for this possibility. But now in WtF there is this whole &quot;Tribe&quot; of wolves, this implies that they too are quite numerous, who reject the normal Tribes and go on it alone and that makes it overall even harder to see a reason for giving up on everything in your old life to join up with a bunch of strangers <b>who have certain sociopathic tendencies.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Tendencies that you would soon discover in yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=439554#post439554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And like said Oath of the Moon doesn't really help the matter either as there is no law in it against killing, except other Werewolves which creates it's own problems when the Blood Talons are a thing, only against eating humans/wolves. That in itself implies, it pretty much downright says, that this is a society where killing is acceptable. And not only that but htey draw the line on eating your victim. Up to and until that point everything is just fine and dandy according to their laws. Now try to take all that in through fresh eyes from a perspective of someone who feels the conflicted emotions of guilt mixed with a feeling of exhilarating freedom and who doesn't know about the bad sides of resisting these urges yet and you should start to see how odd it should feel from an IC perspective. It should feel like your going insane gaining some sick enjoyment from hunting and killing others, colored by the feelings of guilt from your human upbringing, and that these People offering to help have fallen of that wagon a long time ago into accepting their insanity and just letting go. The human reaction is to reach for something familiar and to resist that fall into those feelings that you think as insane. Joining a Tribe seems like an act of letting go and reaching for the unknown which is pretty rare way to go about things.<br /> <br /> I have no difficulties in seeing how nuanced hunting is for the Forsaken, or all the meanings they might put behind the word but then again I have read a manual about them and their kind while the poor recruit has not and he is likely not in a calm enough mood to reflect on all the possible meanings of the word hunt. I am not looking at this from the perspective of a player but of a poor unfortunate character put into that situation.<br /> <br /> But enough of my ramblings I do think I have made my point clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>What else would you expect from a society of werewolves, creatures intelligently designed to kill? This? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ASzFs4_4kvk\" data-code=\"ASzFs4_4kvk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ASzFs4_4kvk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T15:14:54-07:00","id":440518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=439773#post439773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But now in 2ed theyn did, page 64:<br /> &quot;Only a killing blow would do, and so the Uratha \u2014 and five<br /> of the greatest wolf spirits \u2014 went for Urfarah\u2019s throat.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, son of a bitch. I swear I'd read that back when we did our drafts and such, and then obviously I'd forgotten it. I stand corrected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T17:51:15-07:00","id":440680,"title":"","content":"That's just one version of the story, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T17:56:15-07:00","id":440691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=440680#post440680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just one version of the story, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this version brings the question why the 5 Firstborn weren't punished by Luna.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T18:01:59-07:00","id":440699,"title":"","content":"Maybe they <i>were</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T18:03:40-07:00","id":440701,"title":"","content":"Have you seen the babysitting duty they're on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T18:24:13-07:00","id":440737,"title":"","content":"Maybe they weren't hers to punish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T18:50:49-07:00","id":440760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=440691#post440691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And this version brings the question why the 5 Firstborn weren't punished by Luna.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't her children. You can't really punish someone else's kids. And their mothers, being mere wolf spirits, were probably not powerful enough to punish them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T19:53:35-07:00","id":443643,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure I remember this in 1st ed and (less clearly) in this edition as well, but doesn't it say that Father Wolf's death cry killed everyone in the immediate area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T20:12:07-07:00","id":443667,"title":"","content":"In 1e, it was stated that his death howl killed the werewolf who finished him off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T02:45:45-07:00","id":443960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=440518#post440518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, son of a bitch. I swear I'd read that back when we did our drafts and such, and then obviously I'd forgotten it. I stand corrected.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Stew asked me to retell the Sundering in a &quot;this story is true&quot; style. So I deliberately made some changes. Clearly a different Cahalith wrote the 1st ed version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T02:48:38-07:00","id":443961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=443960#post443960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Stew asked me to retell the Sundering in a &quot;this story is true&quot; style. So I deliberately made some changes. Clearly a different Cahalith wrote the 1st ed version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, obviously. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T06:13:53-07:00","id":444077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430767-new-to-forsaken-1-0-and-totally-new-to-2-0-but-what-is-2-0-about?p=439988#post439988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I like to present it is that most newly first changed werewolves don't immediately join a Tribe. The books do say that the Uratha and the Pure keep tabs on wolf blooded who may be on the verge of their first change and approach them right away, but for reasons similar to yours, I don't imagine that would generally be well-received. In my games, the tribes are well aware of that, and tend to leave the new werewolf alone for a few weeks, to give them time to process what's happened and start getting used to their new predatory urges. Obviously, they monitor the pup closely during this time, so they can intervene if they get themselves into trouble, or if the other side tries to get to them first. During this period, the new werewolf is likely a murder suspect, which is sure to add a lot of stress, and potential death rage triggers. Their whole life is falling apart around them, they're seeing spirits that constantly harras them, and all the while they have a near irresistible urge to hunt and to kill. THAT's when the tribes' representatives come to them, and offer purpose, clarity, and a way to realize those predatory urges <i>without</i> hurting people they care about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree with you in the assessment that newly first changed werewolves don't immediately join a Tribe.<br /> <br /> I don't necessarily think that's because some newly first changed werewolves are too cautious, but more that the Tribes prefer to be selective of their membership. If a new werewolf has qualms about hunting other werewolves, then they might be a poor fit for the Blood Talons. If a new werewolf seems to have trouble grokking the tribal ban, then maybe you don't want to bring them in, only to make themselves an embarrassment to the tribe and (possibly more importantly in someone's consideration) their teacher.<br /> <br /> I don't see Tribes as being these well organized and tiered organizations. They're networks of notable werewolves who rise and fall by their reputation. Networks are about knowing people, establishing your own reputation and being willing to share what you know with other people in your network.<br /> <br /> Based on this understanding... I can see a Tribe being willing to tip off another Tribe of a potential recruit. If a Bone Shadow has found a Ghost Wolf that seems interested in joining a greater support network, but still feels like a poor fit to follow Death Wolf's ethos or otherwise seems unsuited to the Bone Shadow tribe, then it doesn't hurt the Bone Shadow to direct that Ghost Wolf to a contact they have in another Tribe as a potential recruit. It's likely that contact will do the same for the Bone Shadow in the future, or it could be an expression of trading favors, such as a promise to teach a Gift later on.<br /> <br /> I kinda think that one of the biggest questions to answer for a new PC that is part of a Tribe is, &quot;Who mentored this character?&quot;<br /> <br /> You don't want to be known as the guy who brought Moon Moon into the Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 03-16-2015, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T09:38:04-07:00","id":444407,"title":"","content":"True, but you also have to balance that against the risk of them joining the Pure or becoming a Bale Hound. A pack might approach a new wolf and offer them support and guidance, but not necessarily recruit them to a Tribe until they've proven their worth. This is also a nice in-character explanation for Tribal Renown - it's not that joining the Blood Talons is particularly glorious in and of itself, it's just that young Uratha who are considering joining the Blood Talons are expected to prove themselves to the Tribe through glorious acts before they can join.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}